       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual 400\u2013800 mg per dose. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no benefit.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day, which is a common dose for inflammatory pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours:** for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf the 1,600 mg figure was a typo, for example for 1,600 mg/day total, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it. If you meant a different drug or a different indication, tell me that too."
      }
